# Peecho API v3

Peecho’s print API enables you to sell digital content as high quality print on demand products. 

Our RESTful API uses standard HTTP methods, authentication protocols and response codes. It accepts data in application/json format and returns all responses in JSON.

<div style="border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 10px; margin: 10px 0; background-color: #f9f9f9;">

<strong>Current version:</strong> API v3 (this documentation)

<strong>Previous version:</strong> <a href="https://peechoapiv2.docs.apiary.io/#">API v2 Documentation</a><p> Note: API v2 is deprecated and will be phased out, though it remains functional for existing integrations.</p> 
</div>



## Getting started 
<p>Our <a href="https://www.peecho.com/blog/how-to-place-your-first-peecho-api-order" target="_blank">step-by-step guide</a> walks you through placing your first API order, covering everything from authentication to submitting orders to our print network.</p>

## Environments
<p>We have two environments: <strong>Test</strong> and <strong>Prod</strong>.</p>

<h4>Test</h4>
<p>Our testing environment allows you to prepare your integration for production.

Orders placed in the test environment <strong> cannot be physically shipped</strong>
 to you or your customers, and you will <strong>not be charged</strong> for using it.
 
 To get started, create an account in the test environment to receive your API key specifically for testing.</p>
<p><strong>Test API:</strong> <a href="https://test.www.peecho.com" target="_blank">https://test.www.peecho.com</a></p>

<h4>Prod</h4>
<p>Prod is our <strong>production</strong> environment. Any orders placed here <strong>must be paid for prior to being produced and shipped</strong>.


To pay for orders, you can purchase credits through your Peecho account.
</p>
<p><strong>Live dashboard:</strong> <a href="https://www.peecho.com" target="_blank">https://www.peecho.com</a></p>

## Authentication
<p>Your API key provides access to the Peecho API. You can find your keys on your dashboard under <strong>Settings > API.</strong></p>
The <strong>Merchant API key</strong> is used by most endpoints for authorization. Some endpoints also require a <strong>Secret key</strong>, which is used for SHA-256 encoding information to provide extra security.</li>
</ul>
<!-- section: Orders -->

## Peecho orders
<p>Peecho orders support multiple items as long as they can be fulfilled by the same production location. This is usually the case for products from the same category. However, you can check if different products can be grouped by using the Quote endpoint (inside the <strong>Check products/offerings endpoint)</strong>. This will return the products that can be ordered together and the ones that need to be quoted and ordered separately.</p>

<p>Creating an order can be done using a single API request, supplying all relevant information. After being created, an API order remains in <strong>Open</strong> state. In this state, you can still update details like the address and print files until you pay for the order. Once paid, Peecho will process the order, prepare the items for production and submit the order to one of our print facilities. <p>


<h3>General order flow</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Order  and items created
  <li>Payment submitted
  <li>Print facility allocated 
  <li>Item files processed 
  <li>Item ready to be printed 
  <li>Order submission to facility
  <li>Production
  <li>Shipping 
</ol>

## Order status
<p>The print on demand order goes through a lifecycle of fulfillment with different stages. For each stage, there is an associated order status.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Status</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>NO_PRINT_FACILITY_ERROR</td>
      <td>No production facility has been assigned to the order.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>OPEN</td>
      <td>The order has been created but not yet paid.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>PAID</td>
      <td>The order has been successfully paid and confirmed.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>PAYMENT_ERROR</td>
      <td>There was a problem processing the payment, often due to insufficient credit or another issue.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>CHECK_ORDER</td>
      <td>The order is being reviewed manually, either by the Peecho team or by you, typically due to missing address details or high value.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>HOLD_ORDER_CHECK</td>
      <td>The order is on hold, awaiting a response from the client.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>WAITING_TO_DISPATCH</td>
      <td>The order is validated and paid, waiting for its items to be processed.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>IN_PRINT_QUEUE</td>
      <td>The order is queued for printing. At this stage, it can no longer be modified.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>SUBMITTED</td>
      <td>The order has been submitted to a production facility by the printer system.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>SUBMISSION_ERROR</td>
      <td>An error occurred while submitting the order to the production facility.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>IN_PRODUCTION</td>
      <td>The order is currently being produced.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>PRODUCTION_ERROR</td>
      <td>An error occurred during the production process.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>SHIPPED</td>
      <td>The order has been shipped to the customer.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>CANCELLED</td>
      <td>The order has been cancelled.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>REFUNDED</td>
      <td>The order has been refunded.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

## Item status
<p>Each item within an order has its own item status, which reflects the current stage of the item in its processing lifecycle.</p>


<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Status</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>AWAITING_PAYMENT</td><td>The order has been created but not yet paid.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PENDING_COMPLETION</td><td>The item is waiting for files (applies to asynchronous orders created without files).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PING_BACK_ERROR</td><td>An error occurred while sending a pingback to your service.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>QUEUED_FOR_PROCESSING</td><td>The file has been queued for processing.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CHECK_PROCESSING_ERROR</td><td>There was an issue processing the file. Peecho will review the issue and contact you if necessary.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PROCESSING</td><td>The file is currently being processed.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PROCESSED</td><td>The file was successfully processed. It will either be moderated (by you or Peecho) or sent directly to the printer.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CHECK_ITEM</td><td>The file requires moderation due to an issue. Review is needed by support or your team.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>HOLD_ITEM_CHECK</td><td>The item is on hold and awaiting a client response.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>PRINT_READY</td><td>The file was processed successfully and is ready for production.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

## Peecho error codes
<p>Error responses may contain a specific error code. Descriptions of the problem and suggested solutions can be found in the table below.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Code</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>APP_FORBIDDEN</td><td>Incorrect API key provided. Check your API key in the API section of any application in your dashboard.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>APP_NO_COMP_DETAILS</td><td>Company details are required for tax calculations. Set them on your application's Settings page.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>COLOR_INVALID</td><td>Invalid color format. Colors must be specified in hex format, e.g. #RRGGBB.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CURR_INVALID</td><td>Invalid currency code. Supported currencies include: USD, JPY, BGN, CZK, DKK, ILS, GBP, HUF, LTL, LVL, PLN, RON, SEK, CHF, NOK, HRK, RUB, TRY, AUD, BRL, CAD, CNY, HKD, IDR, INR, KRW, MXN, MYR, NZD, PHP, SGD, THB, ZAR, ISK.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>FONT_INVALID</td><td>Unsupported font for spine text. Available fonts: Arial, Brandon, DarkCourier, Georgia, GochiHand, Helvetica, Tahoma, TimesNewRoman, Verdana.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>INVALID_DATA</td><td>The request contains invalid or missing fields. This may involve format violations, invalid enum values or malformed data.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>MERCH_INSUFFICIENT_BALANCE</td><td>Insufficient account balance. Visit your dashboard to manage payment methods or add credits.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>MULTI_ORDER_INVALID_DATA</td><td>The selected products cannot be fulfilled by the same production facility.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>NO_PF</td><td>No production facility is available to ship the selected product to the chosen country. Use the Offerings endpoint to check product availability by region.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>OFF_MIN</td><td>The requested product has a minimum order quantity. Use the <code>/offering/list</code> endpoint to check product details.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>OFF_NOT_FOUND</td><td>The requested product or offering was not found.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ORD_CANCEL_STATE</td><td>The order cannot be cancelled. This happens if it has already been sent to production (statuses: IN_PRINT_QUEUE, IN_PRODUCTION, SHIPPED) or if it was already cancelled or refunded. Check the status in the Dashboard or using the status endpoint.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ORD_DUPLICATE</td><td>The order reference must be unique per merchant, even across multiple applications.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ORD_FILES_STATE</td><td>Files can only be updated if the order is in the OPEN or PENDING_COMPLETION state. Check the status in the Dashboard or using the status endpoint.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ORD_MISS_ADDR</td><td>A shipping address must be set before payment. Use the Update address endpoint.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ORD_NO_PRINTER</td><td>The order hasn’t been assigned to a production facility. This usually means the address is missing or unsupported. Use the Offerings endpoint to check where a product can be produced.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ORD_PAID_STATE</td><td>Orders can only be marked as PAID if their current status is OPEN or PAYMENT_ERROR. Check the status in the Dashboard or using the status endpoint.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ORD_SECRET</td><td>Incorrect secret provided. It must be the SHA-256 hex-encoded value of your secret key joined with the order ID.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>SPINE_ORDER_NOT_FOUND</td><td>No order found with the specified ID. If you’re calculating spine width for a future order, use the Spine endpoint instead.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

## Peecho payment solutions
<h4> Payment endpoint using credits</h4>
<p>To pay for an API order, submit a request to the Payment endpoint. Before doing so, make sure you have enough credits in your account – credits are required to confirm and fulfill orders.</p>
<p>You can purchase credits from your test dashboard by going to Settings > API > Credit > Buy Credit. The Peecho test environment supports various mock payment methods, including  <a href="https://docs.stripe.com/testing" target="_blank">Stripe testing cards.</a></p>
<p>After acquiring credits and configuring your order, call the Order payment endpoint to confirm the order and send it to production.</p>


<h4>Checkout</h4>
<p><a href="https://www.peecho.com/solutions/checkout" target="_blank">Peecho's checkout</a> requires the creation of a product listing (publication). It provides an easy, cost-free way to sell print on demand products without needing your own webshop. The checkout is customizable and conversion-optimized, designed to help you start selling quickly with minimal setup.</p>

<h4>Coupon codes</h4>
<p>Customers can apply coupon codes during checkout. You can create these coupons using the credits in your Peecho account. The coupon value will be deducted from your available credit balance.</p>

## Webhooks
<p>You can set callback URLs in your application settings under <strong>Settings > API > Webhooks</strong>.</p>

## Status update URL

<p>Triggered whenever an order changes its status.


Signature is the SHA256 encoded value of the secretKey+order_id string

Method: <strong>POST</strong>

Content: <strong>application/json</strong>

Payload:
{
 "signature": "4bf65a3ffc022f0070babee6540048dfc1a3faad270f62f8084fe66f94ebf8fd",
   <p> "order_id": "1234",</p>
   <p> "order_reference": "LL1123",</p>
   <p> "old_status": "IN_PRODUCTION",</p>
   <p> "new_status": "SHIPPED",</p>
   <p> "tracking_code": "XXXXXXX1234",</p>
   <p> "tracking_url": "https://nolp.dhl.de/nextt-online-public/en/search?piececode=XXXXXXX1234"
}</p>


